        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f8de90be-7f5f-54ec-b7a9-cb3bc6428848",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: The Strongest Man in the World, Candleshoe, Now You See Him, Now You Don't, The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes\n- People: Kurt Russell, Jodie Foster, David Niven, Helen Hayes, Leo McKern, John Alderson, Michael Innes\n- Organizations: Disney, Walt Disney Productions\n- Places: Medfield College\n- Topics: film sequels, acting careers\n\nFacts:\n- The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes was released in 1969.\n- Now You See Him, Now You Don't is a sequel to the 1969 film The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes.\n- The Strongest Man in the World was released in 1975 as a Disney film.\n- The Strongest Man in the World stars Kurt Russell as a student at the fictional Medfield College.\n- Candleshoe was released in 1977 as an American family adventure film produced by Walt Disney Productions.\n- Candleshoe is based on Michael Innes's novel Christmas at Candleshoe.\n- Candleshoe stars Jodie Foster, David Niven, Helen Hayes, and Leo McKern.\n- Helen Hayes's role in Candleshoe was her last big-screen appearance.\n- Now You See Him, Now You Don't was followed by The Strongest Man in the World.\n- John Alderson was an English actor born on 10 April 1916 and died on 4 August 2006.\n- John Alderson played the lead in the 1957–58 syndicated western television series Boots and Saddles, which ran for thirty-eight episodes in a single season.\n- John Alderson had an acting career from 1951 to 1990 and appeared in supporting film roles including Candleshoe in 1977.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
